# Line endings.
#
# This repository is edited on Windows and executed on Linux. Git's
# core.autocrlf=true converts working-copy files to CRLF, and for a shell
# script that is not a formatting preference — it is a broken deployment:
#
#     sudo ./write-env.sh
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# and, more insidiously when the script is invoked as `bash script.sh` so the
# shebang is never read, every assignment silently gains a trailing carriage
# return. VALUE=true becomes "true\r", which compares equal to nothing and
# turns a working configuration into an inexplicable one.
#
# Anything the Linux host executes or parses byte-for-byte is pinned to LF
# here, regardless of the developer's autocrlf setting.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf

# Compose and CI read these, and while both tolerate CRLF, a heredoc inside
# them does not.
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# nginx includes these verbatim.
*.conf          text eol=lf

# Served to browsers and packaged into the Android APK; keeping them LF keeps
# the bytes identical between the website and the app bundle.
*.py            text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf

# Binary, never converted. The font files in particular are corrupted by any
# byte substitution, and a corrupted Tamil font produces a petition of empty
# boxes.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.webp          binary
*.heic          binary
*.pdf           binary
*.ttf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.docx          binary
*.xlsx          binary
*.pptx          binary
*.sqlite        binary
*.jks           binary
*.keystore      binary
